          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"E\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R2\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Q2 is permanently turned on, pulling Q1's gate low and keeping the fan power output enabled regardless of PWM. The direct VCC-to-GND path through Q2's base-emitter junction can cause excessive base current and damage Q2 or the supply.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: Q2's base is tied directly to VCC while its emitter is tied to GND, and the PWM signal is not connected to the base, so the high-side PMOS switch is permanently on and the NPN driver is effectively shorted to the supply."
}

